   "min": 6,
   "screens": [
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Spanish speaker alert",
     "title": "Why a phonetic alphabet?",
     "paras": [
      "On the radio, B, D, P, T and V sound the same. And Spanish speakers mix <b>E</b> and <b>I</b>: English <b>E</b> sounds like Spanish <i>i</i>.",
      "So on board you never say letters. You say words: <b>Echo</b>, <b>India</b>."
     ]
    },
